chapters.clear()
add('chemistry',1,'laboratory','Laboratory skills and scientific investigation',[1,2,7,8,9],[
'Chemistry investigates substances, their properties and the changes they undergo. It connects with farming through fertilisers and soils, health through medicines and diagnostics, industry through materials and fuels, and environmental work through water and pollution analysis. A benefit must be considered alongside safe handling and waste disposal; producing a useful substance does not make every use harmless.',
'A laboratory is a controlled workplace, not a place to taste or casually mix substances. Read instructions before starting, wear the required eye protection and clothing, tie back long hair and keep exits clear. Report broken apparatus, spills and injuries promptly. Never pipette by mouth. Heating, concentrated chemicals, unfamiliar reactions and fire response require a teacher or competent supervisor. In an emergency, alert the responsible adult and follow the school emergency procedure instead of improvising a chemical treatment.',
'Choose apparatus to match the task. A beaker holds and mixes liquids but is not usually the best instrument for an accurate volume. A measuring cylinder measures liquid volume more closely; a balance measures mass. A funnel supports transfer or filtration, a test tube holds small samples and a thermometer measures temperature. Inspect apparatus for damage and read scales at an appropriate eye level. Where a clear liquid forms a curved surface, the bottom of the meniscus is commonly read at eye level; the instrument and liquid determine the correct convention.',
'An investigation begins with a clear question and a testable prediction. Change the independent variable, observe or measure the dependent variable, and keep relevant controlled variables similar. Repeat observations to identify variation, record units and distinguish observations from conclusions. A fair test of dissolving rate could vary water temperature while keeping water volume, solute mass, particle size and stirring conditions comparable. A result supports a conclusion only within the tested conditions.'],[
'Question: Does temperature affect dissolving time? Independent variable: temperature. Dependent variable: time to dissolve. Controls include water volume and solute amount. Do not change temperature and stirring at the same time.',
'A beaker suggests about 50 mL while a suitable measuring cylinder allows a finer reading. Choose the cylinder for a volume measurement and a balance if the task asks for mass.',
'Observation: a solid remains on the filter. Conclusion: an insoluble component was retained. The observation alone does not identify the substance or prove the filtrate is safe to drink.'],
{'independent variable':'The factor deliberately changed in an investigation.','dependent variable':'The measured or observed response.','meniscus':'The curved surface of a liquid in a container.'},[
('Name two areas where chemistry is useful.','Agriculture and health; industry or environmental monitoring are also valid.','Link each area to an example.'),('Which apparatus measures mass?','A balance.','A measuring cylinder measures volume.'),('Which is more suitable for measuring 35 mL: a beaker or measuring cylinder?','A suitable measuring cylinder.','Its scale is intended for volume measurement.'),('What is the independent variable in a temperature–dissolving investigation?','Water temperature.','It is the deliberately changed factor.'),('What can be the dependent variable in that investigation?','Time taken for the stated amount to dissolve.','Specify a measurable response.'),('Give two controlled variables for the investigation.','Water volume and solute mass; particle size and stirring are also relevant.','Keep other influential conditions similar.'),('Why repeat observations?','To detect variation and improve confidence in the pattern.','Repeats do not justify inventing identical results.'),('State one rule about tasting chemicals.','Never taste laboratory chemicals.','They are not safe foods.'),('What should happen after an injury or serious spill?','Alert the responsible adult and follow the school emergency procedure.','Do not improvise chemical first aid.'),('State one use of a funnel.','Transferring liquids or supporting filtration.','Match the tool to a specific function.'),('Why must units accompany numerical measurements?','They identify the quantity scale and allow interpretation and comparison.','A bare number is incomplete.'),('Explain the difference between observation and conclusion.','An observation records what was seen or measured; a conclusion interprets the evidence.','Give a linked example.'),('Why should broken glassware not be used?','It can break further, leak or injure someone.','Report it for safe handling.'),('What is a testable prediction?','A statement of an expected outcome that observations can support or challenge.','It must connect to a measurable investigation.'),('Why does a clear filtrate not prove purity?','Dissolved substances may remain even when particles are not visible.','Clarity and chemical purity are different.')],['Choose apparatus and read measurements appropriately.','Plan a controlled investigation.','Follow laboratory and emergency boundaries.'])
add('physics',1,'data-investigation','Measurements, graphs and experimental evidence',[8,9,11,12,13,14,15,16],[
'A useful measurement states a quantity, a numerical value and a unit. Select an instrument with a suitable range and resolution: a metre rule for ordinary length, a stopwatch for time, a balance for mass and a measuring cylinder for liquid volume. The smallest scale division influences how finely the result can be read. More decimal digits do not automatically mean a more accurate measurement.',
'Check zero readings and view scales carefully. A zero error shifts readings even when nothing should register. Parallax results from viewing a scale from the wrong angle. Repeated readings can reveal random variation, but repeating a biased method does not remove systematic error. Record what was actually observed, including an unexpected value; investigate a suspected mistake rather than quietly replacing it.',
'Organise data in a table with a clear heading and units for each column. The mean is the sum of values divided by their number; the range is maximum minus minimum. Values should be combined only when they describe comparable quantities and conditions. A missing reading is not zero. A large difference between repeats is a reason to examine technique, timing or conditions.',
'Graphs show relationships. Put the independent variable on the horizontal axis and the dependent variable on the vertical axis unless the task specifies otherwise. Choose convenient scales, label units and plot points accurately. A best-fit line or curve represents the overall pattern rather than forcing every point into a zigzag. The gradient is vertical change divided by horizontal change, with units inherited from both axes. State the limits of what the graph supports; extrapolating far beyond observations can be unreliable.'],[
'Time readings 12.1 s, 11.9 s and 12.0 s have mean 36.0/3=12.0 s and range 0.2 s. Retain the unit in both results.',
'A distance–time line passes through (2 s,6 m) and (6 s,18 m). Gradient=(18−6)/(6−2)=3 m/s, representing speed for that straight section.',
'A balance reads 2 g when empty. This suggests a zero error; simply averaging many similarly shifted readings will not remove that bias.'],
{'resolution':'The smallest change distinguishable by a measuring instrument.','systematic error':'A consistent measurement bias associated with the method or instrument.','best-fit line':'A line representing the overall pattern of plotted observations.'},[
('Which instrument measures mass?','A balance.','Use an instrument matched to the quantity.'),('What is meant by instrument range?','The span of values it can measure appropriately.','The required reading should fit within that span.'),('What is parallax error?','A reading error caused by viewing a scale from an unsuitable angle.','Align the eye appropriately.'),('A balance reads 3 g when empty. What type of issue is suggested?','Zero error.','A consistent offset can bias all readings.'),('Find the mean of 9, 10 and 11 s.','10 s','Add 30 and divide by three.'),('Find the range of 4.2, 4.5 and 4.3 cm.','0.3 cm','Maximum minus minimum.'),('Why is a missing reading different from zero?','Missing means unobserved; zero would claim a real measured value.','Do not fabricate data.'),('Which graph axis commonly shows the independent variable?','Horizontal axis.','Label its quantity and unit.'),('Give the formula for gradient.','Change in vertical quantity divided by change in horizontal quantity.','Use two suitable points on the line.'),('Find gradient from (1 s,2 m) to (5 s,10 m).','2 m/s','(10−2)/(5−1).'),('Why use a best-fit line rather than a zigzag through every reading?','It describes the overall relationship without treating each random variation as a real change in trend.','The graph should fit the evidence sensibly.'),('Can repeated readings alone remove a systematic error?','No. The underlying bias needs to be identified and corrected.','Averaging is not a cure for every error.'),('What should a table column heading include?','The measured quantity and unit.','Place repeated units in the heading where appropriate.'),('Why can extrapolation be unreliable?','The relationship may change outside the observed range.','Distinguish observation from prediction.'),('Why are extra decimal digits not proof of accuracy?','They may exceed the instrument resolution or hide a bias.','Precision of notation is not evidence of closeness to the true value.')],['Select suitable measurement tools.','Calculate and interpret means and ranges.','Present evidence in labelled tables and graphs.'])
add('biology',1,'classification','Classification, organisms and microscopes',[1,4,5,6,7],[
'Biology studies living organisms and their processes. Classification groups organisms using selected characteristics so that similarities, differences and relationships can be studied and information communicated. An artificial system may use a few convenient visible traits; a natural system aims to reflect a broader set of relationships. One superficial similarity does not prove close relationship: a bird and an insect both fly but differ in many major features.',
'Scientific names reduce confusion between local names. In binomial naming, the first word is the genus and begins with a capital letter; the second is the specific epithet and begins with a lower-case letter. Both are written in italics in print or separately underlined when handwritten. Homo sapiens is an example. A species name is the two-word combination, not the second word alone.',
'The school classification framework in this syllabus includes Monera, Protista, Fungi, Plantae and Animalia, with viruses considered separately. Monera includes organisms such as bacteria that lack a membrane-bound nucleus. Protists are diverse; fungi absorb nutrients and do not photosynthesise like green plants. Most familiar plants make food by photosynthesis, while animals ingest organic food. Viruses are not cellular organisms and reproduce only within host cells. Modern classification systems may organise these groups differently, so identify the framework being used.',
'A microscope makes small structures visible, but good use requires preparation. Begin with low power, place and secure the slide, illuminate appropriately and focus without striking the slide with the objective. Total magnification is eyepiece magnification multiplied by objective magnification. Keep observations separate from assumptions about identity. Draw clear labelled structures actually seen; do not add organelles simply because a textbook diagram includes them. Slides and biological material should be prepared and handled under the required school guidance.'],[
'For a 10× eyepiece and 4× objective, total magnification=10×4=40×. Changing to a 10× objective gives 100×.',
'A wing is not enough to classify an animal as a bird: insects also have wings. Consider body organisation and other features before deciding.',
'Write Homo sapiens, not homo Sapiens. The genus starts with a capital; the specific epithet starts lower case, and the full name is treated as a two-word unit.'],
{'classification':'Grouping organisms by selected characteristics and relationships.','genus':'The first taxonomic word in a binomial scientific name.','magnification':'The factor by which an image’s linear size exceeds the object’s size.'},[
('Why classify organisms?','To organise information and study similarities, differences and relationships.','It is more than making a list of names.'),('Which word begins with a capital in a binomial name?','The genus.','The specific epithet begins lower case.'),('Correct the capitalisation: homo Sapiens.','Homo sapiens','The two words together form the species name.'),('How are binomial names indicated in print?','In italics.','Handwritten names are separately underlined.'),('Why is flying alone a poor test for a bird?','Insects and other organisms can also fly.','Use several meaningful features.'),('Which syllabus group includes bacteria?','Monera, in the school framework used here.','Modern systems may use different groupings.'),('Do typical bacteria have a membrane-bound nucleus?','No.','Their organisation differs from eukaryotic cells.'),('How do fungi commonly obtain nutrients?','By absorbing dissolved nutrients after external digestion.','They do not make food by photosynthesis like green plants.'),('Are viruses made of cells?','No.','They are considered separately from cellular organisms.'),('Where can viruses reproduce?','Within suitable host cells.','They depend on host-cell machinery.'),('Find total magnification for a 10× eyepiece and 40× objective.','400×','Multiply eyepiece and objective values.'),('Why begin microscope observation at low power?','It helps locate the specimen and focus with a wider field and safer working distance.','Move to higher power appropriately.'),('State one reason not to force an objective towards the slide.','It can damage the lens or slide.','Focus using the correct procedure.'),('What should a biological drawing represent?','Structures actually observed, with clear labels.','Do not invent unseen detail.'),('Distinguish an artificial from a natural classification approach.','Artificial classification uses selected convenient traits; natural classification aims to reflect broader relationships.','State the basis rather than merely naming the systems.')],['Use scientific names correctly.','Compare major school-level organism groups.','Calculate magnification and follow observation conventions.'])
add('mathematics',1,'lines-equations','Simultaneous equations and straight lines',[13,14,15,16,17,18,19,20],[
'Two simultaneous equations describe conditions that must hold for the same unknowns. A solution pair must satisfy both equations, not just one. Substitution replaces a variable with an equivalent expression from the other equation. Elimination adds or subtracts suitable multiples so one variable cancels. Keep equality by applying the same operation to both sides.',
'For x+y=11 and x−y=3, adding gives 2x=14, so x=7 and y=4. Check 7+4=11 and 7−4=3. If equations are proportional, they may describe the same line and have infinitely many solution pairs; if they are inconsistent, there is no common solution. Not every pair of linear equations has exactly one solution.',
'Coordinates (x,y) locate a point using horizontal and vertical positions relative to chosen axes. For a line through distinct points, gradient m=(y₂−y₁)/(x₂−x₁), provided x₂≠x₁. In y=mx+c, m is gradient and c the vertical-axis intercept. A vertical line has undefined finite gradient in this formula and is written x=a, not y=mx+c with an ordinary numerical m.',
'To draw a line, choose convenient x values, calculate the corresponding y values and plot at least two points accurately. Their intersection can show a simultaneous solution. The accuracy depends on scale and plotting; use algebra to obtain an exact result when possible. For inequalities, remember to reverse the sign when multiplying or dividing by a negative number. A solution interval contains many values, not just one number at its boundary.'],[
'Solve x+y=9 and x−y=1. Add: 2x=10, x=5; substitute to get y=4. Both equations are satisfied.',
'For points (1,4) and (3,10), gradient=(10−4)/(3−1)=3. Using y=3x+c and (1,4), c=1, so the line is y=3x+1.',
'Solve −2x+3>11. Subtract 3: −2x>8; divide by −2 and reverse the inequality: x<−4. For example x=−5 gives 13>11.'],
{'simultaneous solution':'Values satisfying all the stated equations at the same time.','gradient':'Vertical change divided by horizontal change along a line.','intercept':'A point or coordinate where a graph crosses a stated axis.'},[
('Solve x+y=10 and x−y=2.','x=6, y=4.','Add equations, then substitute.'),('Solve x+y=7 and y=2x−2.','x=3, y=4.','Substitute y into the first equation.'),('Solve 2x+y=13 and x+y=8.','x=5, y=3.','Subtract the equations.'),('Why check a solution pair in both equations?','It must satisfy both conditions simultaneously.','One equation alone is insufficient.'),('Find gradient through (0,1) and (2,5).','2','(5−1)/(2−0).'),('State gradient and y-intercept in y=−3x+4.','Gradient −3; intercept 4.','Read the correctly arranged form.'),('Find y when x=3 in y=2x−5.','1','2×3−5.'),('Does (2,7) lie on y=3x+1?','Yes.','3×2+1=7.'),('What is the equation of a vertical line through x=4?','x=4','Every point on it has that x-coordinate.'),('What is the gradient of a horizontal line?','0','Its vertical change is zero.'),('Solve 3x−2≤10.','x≤4','Add 2 then divide by positive 3.'),('Solve −5x≥15.','x≤−3','Reverse the sign on division by −5.'),('What does the intersection of two line graphs represent?','A coordinate pair satisfying both line equations.','Read both coordinates.'),('Can two distinct parallel lines have a simultaneous solution?','No.','They have no common point.'),('Find the equation with gradient 2 passing through (0,−3).','y=2x−3','The given point is the y-intercept.')],['Solve and check simultaneous equations.','Calculate gradients and line equations.','Interpret graphical solutions and inequalities.'])
add('kiswahili',1,'kusoma-kamusi','Kusoma kwa uelewa, msamiati na kamusi',[5,6,7,8,9,10,11,12,13],[
'Usomaji wenye uelewa unahusisha kutambua ujumbe mkuu, taarifa saidizi na uhusiano wa mawazo. Kabla ya kusoma, angalia kichwa na kusudi la kazi. Unaposoma, zingatia alama za uandishi na muktadha wa maneno. Kusoma kwa sauti kunahitaji kasi inayoeleweka na kiimbo kinachoendana na tungo, lakini kuigiza sauti bila kuelewa maana hakutoshi.',
'Soma matini hii asilia: Mwanaidi alikopa kamusi maktabani ili kuandaa maonesho ya darasa. Alipokutana na neno lisilojulikana, hakuchukua maana ya kwanza tu. Alisoma maana tofauti na kuangalia sentensi aliyokuwa akiandika. Baadaye alimwonyesha Baraka rasimu yake. Baraka alipendekeza afafanue maneno mawili ambayo yangeweza kuwachanganya wasikilizaji. Walipomaliza, walirudisha kamusi kwa wakati na kuweka nakala ya maelezo yao kwenye ubao wa darasa.',
'Kamusi hupanga vidahizo kwa utaratibu maalumu, mara nyingi wa alfabeti. Kidadisi cha neno kinaweza kuonyesha tahajia, aina ya neno, maana zaidi ya moja, mfano wa matumizi na taarifa nyingine. Taarifa hutofautiana kwa aina ya kamusi. Chagua maana inayolingana na muktadha; si kila maana inafaa kila sentensi. Katika mawasiliano ya kidijitali, tumia kamusi au chanzo kinachotambulika badala ya kuamini tafsiri ya kwanza bila kukagua.',
'Muhtasari wa matini huchagua hoja kuu na kuziunganisha kwa lugha yako bila kuongeza tukio jipya. Katika mazungumzo, sikiliza hadi uelewe hoja kabla ya kujibu, toa nafasi kwa wengine na uliza ufafanuzi kwa heshima. Kumbukumbu fupi zinaweza kusaidia kufuatilia mawazo, lakini zisigeuze maoni ya mtu kuwa ukweli uliothibitishwa. Mazoezi haya yanaweza kufanywa kwa kusoma matini; mazoezi halisi ya kusikiliza yanahitaji sauti au msomaji.'],[
'Kwa nini Mwanaidi hakuchukua maana ya kwanza tu? Kwa sababu alitaka maana inayolingana na sentensi na kusudi lake. Jibu linatokana na matini.',
'Mpangilio wa alfabeti: amani, bahari, darasa, elimu. Linganisha herufi ya kwanza; ikiwa inafanana, endelea kwenye herufi zinazofuata.',
'Muhtasari: Mwanaidi alitumia kamusi kwa kuzingatia muktadha, akaboresha rasimu kwa msaada wa Baraka na kurudisha kitabu kwa wakati. Hakuna taarifa kwamba alinunua kamusi.'],
{'kidahizo':'Neno au kipashio kinachoingizwa kama kichwa cha taarifa katika kamusi.','muktadha':'Mazingira ya matumizi yanayosaidia kuelewa maana.','tahajia':'Namna sahihi ya kuandika neno kwa herufi zake.'},[
('Mwanaidi alikopa nini?','Kamusi.','Tumia taarifa iliyotolewa.'),('Alitumia kamusi kwa kusudi gani?','Kuandaa maonesho ya darasa.','Usibuni mtihani au safari.'),('Kwa nini aliangalia sentensi kabla ya kuchagua maana?','Ili achague maana inayolingana na muktadha.','Maana ya kwanza si lazima iwe inayofaa.'),('Baraka alipendekeza nini?','Kufafanua maneno mawili yaliyoweza kuwachanganya wasikilizaji.','Rejelea msaada uliotajwa.'),('Je, matini inasema kamusi ilinunuliwa?','Hapana; ilikopwa.','Tofautisha taarifa na dhana.'),('Panga alfabeti: elimu, bahari, amani.','amani, bahari, elimu.','Linganisha herufi kwa mpangilio.'),('Kidahizo ni nini?','Neno au kipashio kinachotanguliza taarifa yake katika kamusi.','Usikichanganye na mfano wa sentensi pekee.'),('Taja taarifa mbili zinazoweza kupatikana katika kamusi.','Maana na tahajia; aina ya neno au mfano wa matumizi pia ni sahihi.','Taarifa hutegemea kamusi husika.'),('Kwa nini maana ya neno ichaguliwe kwa muktadha?','Neno linaweza kuwa na maana tofauti zinazofaa matumizi tofauti.','Tumia mfano ukihitajika.'),('Andika muhtasari wa sentensi moja wa matini.','Mwanaidi alitumia kamusi kwa makini, akaboresha rasimu na kuirudisha kwa wakati.','Hifadhi hoja kuu bila kuongeza matukio.'),('Taja alama inayofaa mwisho wa swali.','Alama ya kuuliza (?).','Ihusishe na tungo ya swali.'),('Tunga ombi la heshima la ufafanuzi.','Samahani, naomba ueleze zaidi maana ya neno hili.','Uwe na heshima na lengo wazi.'),('Kwa nini kuwapa wengine nafasi ni muhimu kwenye mjadala?','Huwezesha kusikiliza hoja na kushiriki kwa haki.','Si kila mtu anayekatiza huwa ameongeza hoja.'),('Je, matini iliyoandikwa peke yake ni sauti ya kusikiliza?','Hapana; shughuli ya kusikiliza inahitaji sauti au msomaji.','Tofautisha njia za kujifunza.'),('Taja tabia ya Mwanaidi inayoonyesha uwajibikaji.','Alirudisha kamusi kwa wakati.','Toa ushahidi wa matini.')],['Soma matini na toa majibu yenye ushahidi.','Chagua maana sahihi kwa msaada wa kamusi.','Andika muhtasari na shiriki mazungumzo kwa heshima.'])
add('geography',1,'surface-features','Geography, landforms, water bodies and vegetation',[1,3],[
'Geography studies places, environments and relationships between people and the Earth. Physical geography examines features and processes such as landforms, water and climate; human geography considers activities such as settlement, farming, transport and trade. These branches overlap: a river affects settlement and transport, while land use can affect the river’s water quality. Maps, field observations and photographs help investigate such relationships.',
'The commonly used seven-continent model names Africa, Antarctica, Asia, Europe, North America, South America and Australia. Different naming conventions may refer to the wider region of Oceania, so state the model being used. The five commonly recognised oceans are the Pacific, Atlantic, Indian, Southern and Arctic. Tanzania lies on the eastern side of Africa with a coast on the Indian Ocean. A continent is a large landmass; an ocean is a major body of salt water.',
'Relief describes variations in the height and shape of the land. A mountain rises prominently above nearby land; a plateau is an elevated area with a relatively broad level surface; a plain has relatively low relief; a valley is an elongated depression. Definitions describe patterns rather than a guarantee that every surface fits one perfect shape. In Tanzania, Mount Kilimanjaro is a prominent mountain and the surrounding lower land has different relief characteristics.',
'Inland water bodies include lakes, rivers, wetlands and reservoirs. Lake Victoria, Lake Tanganyika and Lake Nyasa/Malawi are major East African lakes shared across national borders. Rivers flow through drainage basins and can connect upstream activities with downstream effects. Vegetation zones reflect interacting influences including rainfall, temperature, soils, altitude, fire and human activity. Forest, woodland, grassland/savanna and sparse dryland vegetation are broad categories; boundaries vary rather than forming identical bands everywhere.',
'A geographical explanation links a feature to its significance with evidence. Plains may make some transport routes easier, but floods or soft soils can still create difficulties. Mountains can influence rainfall, water sources and tourism, but also bring steep-slope hazards. Treat a benefit or challenge as dependent on place and conditions. During observation, record location, visible features and human activities without entering unsafe water, unstable slopes or restricted land.'],[
'A coastal settlement may depend on fishing and transport links. Explaining it well combines a physical setting, human activities and evidence rather than calling it only physical or only human geography.',
'Classify three features: Mount Kilimanjaro is a mountain, Lake Tanganyika an inland lake and the Indian Ocean a major ocean. They are not interchangeable kinds of water/land feature.',
'If bare soil appears after vegetation is removed, investigate runoff, slope and rainfall before predicting erosion. The vegetation change is one part of a connected system, not a complete explanation alone.'],
{'relief':'The variation in height and shape of land.','plateau':'A relatively broad elevated area with a generally level surface.','drainage basin':'An area whose water drains towards a river system or common outlet.'},[
('What does geography study?','Places, environments and relationships between people and the Earth.','Include relationships, not just names of places.'),('Give one physical and one human geography topic.','Landforms and settlement, respectively.','Explain which aspect each examines.'),('Name the ocean bordering mainland Tanzania to the east.','Indian Ocean.','Locate Tanzania on eastern Africa.'),('List three continents in the seven-continent model.','Africa, Asia and Europe; any three correct continents.','Do not list an ocean as a continent.'),('Name the five commonly recognised oceans.','Pacific, Atlantic, Indian, Southern and Arctic.','Use the five-ocean model stated in the lesson.'),('What is relief?','Variation in the height and shape of land.','It is not simply the name of one mountain.'),('Distinguish a plateau from a valley.','A plateau is broadly elevated and relatively level; a valley is an elongated depression.','Compare their land shapes.'),('Give one example of an inland water body.','A lake, river, wetland or reservoir.','An ocean is not inland.'),('Name two major lakes partly bordering Tanzania.','Lake Victoria and Lake Tanganyika; Lake Nyasa/Malawi also qualifies.','Recognise shared borders.'),('Give two influences on vegetation.','Rainfall and temperature; soil, altitude, fire or human activity also matter.','Avoid one-factor explanations.'),('What connects upstream and downstream parts of a river system?','Water flow through a drainage basin.','Activities upstream can have downstream effects.'),('Why can a plain still create transport problems?','Flooding, soft soil or other local conditions may complicate movement.','Low relief alone does not guarantee easy transport.'),('Give one way mountains affect people.','They can influence rainfall, water supply, tourism or steep-slope risks.','Explain the link to a human activity.'),('Why are vegetation boundaries not perfectly uniform?','Several interacting environmental and human factors vary across places.','Broad categories simplify complex patterns.'),('What should be recorded during safe field observation?','Location, visible features and relevant human activities, with evidence.','Do not trespass or enter unsafe terrain.')],['Distinguish physical and human geography.','Identify major land and water features.','Explain vegetation and people–environment relationships.'])
add('business',1,'business-planning','Planning and starting a sole-trader enterprise',[2,3],[
'A business plan explains a proposed enterprise: the customer need, product or service, resources, operations, expected costs and revenue, and risks. Planning does not guarantee success, but it makes assumptions visible so they can be tested. An entrepreneur should distinguish an attractive idea from evidence that enough customers will buy at a workable price.',
'Calculate start-up needs separately from running costs. A sewing machine bought to begin tailoring is a start-up asset; thread, rent and transport may recur. Working capital supports day-to-day operations while money is tied up in stock or unpaid sales. If all available cash is spent on equipment, a business may be unable to buy the materials needed to use it.',
'A sole trader can make decisions directly, but personal capacity and resources limit the operation. Check access to skills, time, suppliers, storage and customers. Keep business transactions recorded even when the owner supplies the money. Money taken for personal use is not evidence of a business expense, and cash put in by the owner is not sales revenue.',
'A small trial helps test demand and practical problems. Specify what will count as evidence, such as the number of paid orders, full cost per item and customer feedback. Review quality, waste and complaints as well as sales totals. Before operating, check the requirements that apply to the location and activity with the responsible authorities; a school exercise is not a licence or a financial promise.'],[
'Equipment costs TSh 40,000 and opening materials TSh 15,000. At least TSh 55,000 is needed for those items, before other costs and cash reserves. Counting equipment alone understates the plan.',
'A trader buys ten items at TSh 700 each and spends TSh 1000 on transport. Total batch cost=8000, so relevant unit cost before other expenses is 800. At a selling price of 1000, 200 per sold item remains before other costs.',
'A trial sells six of ten products. Record six sales and four remaining items; do not record ten sales merely because ten were produced. Unsold stock and customer comments both inform the next decision.'],
{'start-up cost':'A cost incurred to establish an enterprise.','working capital':'Resources available for day-to-day business operations.','business plan':'A description of proposed customers, operations, resources, finances and risks.'},[
('What is the purpose of a business plan?','To explain the enterprise and make its assumptions, resources, finances and risks visible.','It supports testing and decisions.'),('Give one start-up asset for a tailor.','A sewing machine.','It is used to begin and continue production.'),('Give one recurring cost for a small shop.','Rent, transport or other running inputs.','Distinguish the period and activity.'),('Why keep working capital after buying equipment?','Materials and daily operations still need resources before receipts arrive.','An asset alone cannot fund every running need.'),('Equipment costs 25,000 and opening materials 12,000. Find their total.','TSh 37,000','Add both items.'),('Eight items cost 500 each and batch transport is 800. Find unit cost before other expenses.','TSh 600','Total4800 divided by eight.'),('At a selling price of 750, what remains per sold item in that example?','TSh 150','750−600; other costs may still apply.'),('Ten items are made and seven sold. How many remain?','3 items.','Production does not equal sales.'),('Is owner money invested in the business sales revenue?','No. It is owner funding.','Keep sources of funds distinct.'),('Is money taken by the owner automatically a business expense?','No. Personal withdrawals are different from business operating costs.','Record the transaction appropriately.'),('State two things to measure in a small trial.','Paid sales and full cost per unit; quality or feedback are also useful.','Use observable evidence.'),('Why investigate suppliers?','Reliable availability, price and quality affect operations.','Do not assume inputs will always arrive as hoped.'),('Does a plan eliminate all risk?','No. Demand, costs and conditions may differ from expectations.','Use the plan to identify and manage uncertainty.'),('Give one possible responsibility towards customers.','Provide truthful product information and address valid quality concerns.','Avoid misleading promises.'),('Why check local requirements before operating?','The activity and location may have applicable rules or obligations.','A classroom exercise does not authorise real operation.')],['Separate start-up resources from operating needs.','Calculate practical small-business costs.','Use a trial and records to improve decisions.'])
add('historia',1,'urithi-ushirikiano','Urithi, maadili na ushirikiano wa jamii',[4,5,6,7,8,9,10],[
'Urithi wa jamii unajumuisha vitu vinavyoonekana kama majengo, maeneo na zana, na mambo yasiyoshikika kama lugha, simulizi, sanaa na maarifa. Urithi hutusaidia kuchunguza maisha ya vizazi vilivyotangulia na kuelewa utambulisho wa sasa. Hata hivyo, maelezo ya urithi yanahitaji ushahidi; simulizi moja au jina la kitu halithibitishi kila dai linalotolewa kuhusu asili yake.',
'Maadili yanahusiana na namna watu wanavyotathmini matendo na wajibu wao kwa wengine. Uaminifu, uwajibikaji, heshima na ushirikiano vinaweza kusaidia kujenga maisha ya pamoja. Mila zinapotathminiwa, zingatia heshima ya binadamu na haki badala ya kudai kwamba kila desturi ya zamani ilikuwa nzuri au kwamba kila jambo jipya ni bora. Jamii zinaweza kuhifadhi maarifa yenye thamani huku zikirekebisha matendo yenye madhara.',
'Utunzaji wa urithi unahitaji ushirikiano wa jamii, wataalamu na mamlaka husika. Usichimbe, kuondoa, kuandika juu au kuuza vitu vya kihistoria bila kufuata taratibu zinazotumika. Kupiga picha au kurekodi maarifa ya mtu kunahitaji kuzingatia ridhaa, faragha na masharti yake. Kuhamisha kitu bila rekodi kunaweza kupoteza muktadha unaosaidia kuelewa matumizi na kipindi chake.',
'Urithi unaweza kusaidia uchumi kupitia ufundi, maonesho, utalii unaowajibika na elimu. Fursa itathminiwe pamoja na manufaa kwa wenye urithi na gharama za kuutunza. Biashara isiwasilishe vitu vipya kama vya kale kwa udanganyifu au kutoa maarifa ya jamii bila heshima. Shughuli za pamoja kama usafi wa mazingira, kujenga huduma na kubadilishana stadi zinaweza kukuza mshikamano na uwezo wa kiuchumi zinapopangwa kwa uwazi na ushiriki wa haki.'],[
'Kikundi cha wanafunzi kinaomba ruhusa ya kusaidia kusafisha eneo la urithi na kinafuata maelekezo ya msimamizi. Huu ni ushiriki unaolenga kuhifadhi, si ruhusa ya kuhamisha vitu vya kale.',
'Mfundi anatengeneza bidhaa mpya kwa kutumia mbinu za jadi. Anaweza kuieleza kama kazi mpya ya ufundi wa jadi, badala ya kudai kwa uongo kwamba ni kitu cha karne zilizopita.',
'Jamii inapoweka rekodi ya mapato na matumizi ya maonesho, wanachama wanaweza kujadili manufaa na gharama kwa ushahidi. Uwazi husaidia uwajibikaji.'],
{'urithi usioshikika':'Lugha, sanaa, simulizi au maarifa yanayorithishwa bila kuwa jengo au kitu kimoja cha kushika.','ridhaa':'Kukubali kwa kuelewa na bila kulazimishwa kushiriki au kuruhusu matumizi fulani.','mshikamano':'Hali ya watu kushirikiana na kuheshimiana katika malengo ya pamoja.'},[
('Taja mifano miwili ya urithi unaoshikika.','Jengo la kihistoria na zana; maeneo au vitu vingine vya kale pia vinafaa.','Taja vitu vinavyoweza kushikwa au kuonekana kama mali.'),('Taja mifano miwili ya urithi usioshikika.','Lugha na simulizi; sanaa au maarifa pia yanafaa.','Si lazima urithi uwe jengo.'),('Kwa nini dai la historia lihitaji ushahidi?','Ili litathminiwe kwa vyanzo na muktadha badala ya kukubaliwa bila uchunguzi.','Dai na uthibitisho si kitu kimoja.'),('Taja maadili mawili yanayosaidia kazi ya pamoja.','Uaminifu na uwajibikaji; heshima na ushirikiano pia ni sahihi.','Eleza namna yanavyosaidia.'),('Je, kila desturi ya zamani ni nzuri bila kutathmini madhara?','Hapana. Heshima ya binadamu na haki vinapaswa kuzingatiwa.','Tathmini matendo badala ya kauli za jumla.'),('Kwa nini upate ridhaa kabla ya kurekodi simulizi?','Kuheshimu haki, faragha na masharti ya mtoa taarifa.','Mtu asishurutishwe.'),('Kwa nini kuondoa kitu cha kale bila rekodi kunaweza kuharibu ushahidi?','Muktadha wa mahali na uhusiano wake na vitu vingine hupotea.','Kitu pekee si taarifa yote.'),('Taja shughuli moja halali ya wanafunzi kusaidia urithi kwa mwongozo.','Usafi ulioidhinishwa au uelimishaji unaofuata maelekezo ya wahusika.','Usipendekeze kuhamisha vitu bila taratibu.'),('Toa mfano wa fursa ya kiuchumi inayohusiana na urithi.','Ufundi au maonesho yanayowajibika.','Husisha manufaa na utunzaji.'),('Kwa nini bidhaa mpya isitambulishwe kwa uongo kuwa ya kale?','Ni udanganyifu unaopotosha wanunuzi na historia.','Tumia maelezo ya kweli.'),('Uwazi wa mapato na matumizi husaidia nini?','Uwajibikaji na uamuzi wenye ushahidi.','Wanachama waweze kuelewa matumizi.'),('Taja mfano wa ushirikiano unaojenga huduma.','Kazi ya pamoja iliyoratibiwa kuboresha mazingira au huduma ya jamii.','Heshimu ushiriki wa haki.'),('Je, utalii pekee ndio matumizi ya urithi?','Hapana; urithi pia una thamani ya elimu, maarifa, sanaa na utambulisho.','Epuka kuupima kwa fedha pekee.'),('Nani wanapaswa kuhusishwa katika utunzaji wa urithi?','Jamii inayohusika, wataalamu na mamlaka zinazofaa.','Wenye uhusiano na urithi wasipuuzwe.'),('Kwa nini fursa ya kiuchumi ipimwe pamoja na gharama za utunzaji?','Mapato ya sasa yanaweza kuandamana na uharibifu au gharama ambazo lazima zidhibitiwe.','Uendelevu unahitaji kuangalia pande zote.')],['Tambua aina na thamani za urithi.','Husisha maadili na utunzaji unaoheshimu watu.','Chunguza fursa na ushirikiano kwa uwajibikaji.'])
add('english',1,'information-letters','Finding information and writing friendly messages',[1,2,12,13,14,18,19,20,21,22,23,33,34,35,36],[
'Information search begins with a clear question. Choose keywords describing the topic and the kind of information needed rather than typing a very long vague sentence. A search engine helps locate sources; it is not itself proof that a result is correct. Look for the author or institution, date, purpose and evidence. In offline practice, compare prepared source cards and decide which would answer a stated question; no internet connection is needed for that exercise.',
'Consider two original source cards. Card A: School library notice, issued Monday, says the library will open at 8 a.m. during revision week. Card B: An undated message says someone heard that all school rooms are closed. For the question about library opening time, Card A is more directly relevant and attributable. It can still be checked with the school if circumstances change. A confident tone and a large number of forwarded messages do not replace a named, relevant source.',
'When learning vocabulary, record the word, its meaning in context and your own example. A word may have more than one meaning: light can refer to illumination or to low weight. A useful vocabulary game pairs words with suitable contexts rather than treating every dictionary meaning as interchangeable. Retelling a story requires a clear sequence; a summary keeps its main events and omits minor detail without inventing an ending.',
'A friendly letter normally includes the sender’s address where required, date, greeting, message and closing. Its tone should suit the relationship and purpose. A clear invitation states the activity, place, date and time and asks for a response where needed. Follow the stages of planning, drafting, revising and editing. A timetable records activities and times consistently so that it can be followed by someone who did not help write it.'],[
'Question: When does the library open during revision week? Useful keywords might be school library revision week opening time. A current school notice is more relevant than an unrelated general article about libraries.',
'Context contrast: The bag is light means not heavy; the lamp gives light means illumination. Use the sentence to choose a meaning.',
'Invitation: Dear Asha, Please join our reading group in the library on Friday at 3 p.m. We will discuss a short story. Let me know whether you can come. Best wishes, Neema. The key practical details are present.'],
{'keyword':'A meaningful search term identifying a topic or information need.','source':'The origin of a statement or information.','revision':'Changing a draft to improve its ideas, organisation or expression.'},[
('What should be clarified before searching for information?','The question and the kind of information needed.','A clear need guides keywords and source choice.'),('Does appearing in search results prove a claim is correct?','No. The source and evidence must still be considered.','A search engine locates material.'),('Which card directly states the library opening time?','Card A.','It is a named school library notice.'),('What is the stated opening time?','8 a.m. during revision week.','Use the detail in the card.'),('What weakens Card B?','It is undated, second-hand and vague about the library.','Identify limitations, not just dislike.'),('Give two things to check about a source.','Author/institution and date; purpose and evidence also matter.','Use information relevant to the question.'),('Write useful keywords for school library opening times.','School library opening time revision week.','Keep relevant terms rather than unrelated words.'),('What does light mean in a light bag?','Not heavy.','Use the sentence context.'),('What does light mean in the lamp gives light?','Illumination.','Do not substitute the weight meaning.'),('Name two useful items in a vocabulary record.','Meaning in context and an original example sentence.','A bare copied word is less useful.'),('What should a story retelling preserve?','The main events and their sequence.','Do not invent events as if they were stated.'),('List four practical details for an invitation.','Activity, place, date and time.','A response request may also be needed.'),('What activity does the model invitation propose?','A reading group discussing a short story.','Do not replace it with an unstated sports event.'),('Name the four writing stages described.','Planning, drafting, revising and editing.','They have different purposes.'),('Why should a timetable be clear to someone else?','It communicates when activities happen and helps people coordinate.','Use consistent times and labels.')],['Search with clear questions and relevant terms.','Evaluate source cards and vocabulary in context.','Write complete friendly messages and invitations.'])
workbook={
'chemistry-f1-laboratory':[('A pupil changes water temperature and stirring speed together. Why is the result difficult to interpret?','Either factor or their combination could affect dissolving time.','Change one intended factor and control relevant alternatives.'),('A beaker reading is 52 mL but its divisions are 10 mL apart. Explain why writing 52.000 mL is unjustified.','The notation implies precision unsupported by the instrument scale.','More digits do not create a finer measurement.'),('Give a report structure for a separation investigation.','Question, method, conditions, observations, results, conclusion and limitations.','Keep observed facts separate from interpretation.')],
'physics-f1-data-investigation':[('Find the mean and range of 5.1, 5.3 and 5.2 s.','Mean5.2 s; range0.2 s.','Add and divide by three; subtract minimum from maximum.'),('A distance–time line passes (2 s,5 m) and (8 s,20 m). Find gradient.','2.5 m/s','(20−5)/(8−2).'),('Why is deleting an unusual reading without explanation poor practice?','It hides evidence and may conceal a real variation or method problem.','Investigate and record any justified correction.')],
'biology-f1-classification':[('Write a correct printed scientific name format using Homo sapiens.','Homo sapiens, italicised, genus capitalised and specific epithet lower case.','Both words form the species name.'),('Find total magnification for 15× eyepiece and 10× objective.','150×','Multiply the two values.'),('Why should an organism not be classified from one convenient trait alone?','Unrelated organisms may share that trait; broader evidence is needed.','Use flying as an example.')],
'mathematics-f1-lines-equations':[('Solve x+y=14 and x−y=4.','x=9,y=5.','Add, then substitute.'),('Find the equation with gradient3 through (0,−2).','y=3x−2','The point gives the vertical intercept.'),('Solve −3x+2<14.','x>−4','Subtract2 then divide by−3 and reverse the sign.')],
'kiswahili-f1-kusoma-kamusi':[('Tunga mfano mmoja wa neno lenye maana zinazobadilika kwa muktadha.','Kichwa kinaweza kuwa sehemu ya mwili au kichwa cha habari.','Sentensi zionyeshe maana zilizokusudiwa.'),('Kwa nini si sahihi kusema Baraka ndiye aliyekopa kamusi?','Matini inasema Mwanaidi aliikopa.','Jibu litegemee ushahidi.'),('Andika ombi la kuuliza maana bila kumkatiza msemaji kwa ukali.','Samahani, ukimaliza naomba ufafanue neno hilo.','Heshimu nafasi na kusudi la mazungumzo.')],
'geography-f1-surface-features':[('Explain how a river can link physical and human geography.','Its flow and landforms affect settlements or farming, while human activity can change its quality.','Show a two-way relationship.'),('Why should a vegetation map be interpreted as broad categories?','Real vegetation varies with several factors and boundaries need not be uniform.','Recognise simplification.'),('Distinguish a lake from an ocean using regional examples.','Lake Tanganyika is inland; the Indian Ocean is a major salt-water ocean.','Use correct feature types.')],
'business-f1-business-planning':[('A trader buys12 items at400 each and transport costs1200. Find relevant unit cost.','TSh500','Total6000 divided by12.'),('A trial produces15 items and sells9. What two quantities should the record distinguish?','Nine sales and six unsold items.','Do not equate output with sales.'),('Why should a trial plan include quality complaints as well as revenue?','Sales alone may conceal problems affecting future demand and responsibilities.','Use more than one performance measure.')],
'historia-f1-urithi-ushirikiano':[('Toa mfano wa matumizi ya urithi yanayohitaji ridhaa.','Kurekodi simulizi au maarifa ya mtoa taarifa.','Heshimu masharti na faragha.'),('Eleza tofauti ya kutengeneza ufundi mpya na kudai kitu ni cha kale.','Kazi mpya inaweza kutumia mbinu za jadi bila kuwa kitu kilichotengenezwa zamani.','Maelezo yawe ya kweli.'),('Kwa nini wenye urithi washirikishwe katika maonesho?','Maamuzi yanawaathiri na wana maarifa na uhusiano muhimu na urithi.','Ushiriki uwe na heshima na uwajibikaji.')],
'english-f1-information-letters':[('Write an invitation that includes a place and time.','Dear Juma, please join us in the library on Tuesday at4 p.m. for a reading session. Let me know if you can attend.','Include the activity and clear arrangements.'),('Which is stronger evidence about school arrangements: a current named notice or an undated rumour? Explain.','The current named notice is more directly attributable and relevant.','Source quality depends on evidence and context.'),('Create two sentences using different meanings of light.','The bag is light. The lamp produces light.','Make each meaning clear from context.')]
}
